1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,129
MAN: <i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,203 --> 00:00:04,330
Where are you, Ed?

3
00:00:04,938 --> 00:00:06,683
What's green and red
and goes round and round?

4
00:00:06,707 --> 00:00:08,300
Zebra with a gaping hole.

5
00:00:08,475 --> 00:00:10,842
Your brilliant mind is as
damaged as the rest of your body.

6
00:00:11,879 --> 00:00:13,142
I guess she was right.

7
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:14,807
You're not smart.

8
00:00:15,148 --> 00:00:17,310
We'd need an army
to take on Penguin.

9
00:00:17,718 --> 00:00:18,879
<i>Makes me miss Falcone.</i>

10
00:00:19,319 --> 00:00:21,865
SOFIA: You came looking for a
gangster, that's exactly what you found.

11
00:00:21,889 --> 00:00:22,889
I'm a Falcone.

12
00:00:22,990 --> 00:00:24,067
I need to know what
you're going to do.

13
00:00:24,091 --> 00:00:25,855
You want the city
back from Penguin,

14
00:00:26,026 --> 00:00:27,026
<i>I'll give that to you.</i>

15
00:00:27,194 --> 00:00:29,527
Did you really think I
wouldn't figure it out?

16
00:00:29,963 --> 00:00:33,331
The two of you have been
whispering like teenagers for weeks.

17
00:00:33,400 --> 00:00:35,130
You never deserved
her in the first place.

18
00:00:36,703 --> 00:00:37,703
Yes, I killed him.

19
00:00:38,071 --> 00:00:39,198
I am sorry.

20
00:00:39,406 --> 00:00:41,307
BRUCE: <i>There's a
legend about this knife.</i>

21
00:00:41,508 --> 00:00:44,034
<i>The man that killed my
grandfather can't have this.</i>

22
00:00:44,211 --> 00:00:45,211
I promise.

23
00:00:45,279 --> 00:00:46,770
<i>That's Ra's al Ghul.</i>

24
00:00:46,947 --> 00:00:49,610
That knife is the
key to everything.

25
00:00:49,883 --> 00:00:51,852
Give me the knife and
I will release the boy.

26
00:00:52,119 --> 00:00:53,599
- Bruce, hand me the knife.
- I can't.

27
00:00:54,021 --> 00:00:55,114
(KNIFE SLICING)

28
00:00:55,789 --> 00:00:56,789
(SCREAMS)

29
00:01:01,061 --> 00:01:04,088
DRIVER: So who's the vegetable?
ORDERLY: Ah, he used to be a gangster.

30
00:01:04,431 --> 00:01:07,560
Name's Gilzean. Maybe Gold?

31
00:01:07,834 --> 00:01:10,702
He took a slug in the noodle.
Been in a coma six months.

32
00:01:10,904 --> 00:01:13,430
So, hospital brass
wants to free up beds?

33
00:01:13,540 --> 00:01:16,738
Yeah. Say take him upstate.

34
00:01:16,810 --> 00:01:17,810
(BOTH LAUGHING RAUCOUSLY)

35
00:01:28,822 --> 00:01:34,193
Rest in Peace, Butch
Gilzean, Cyrus Gold,

36
00:01:35,128 --> 00:01:37,029
(CHUCKLES) whoever
the hell you are.

37
00:01:37,531 --> 00:01:39,557
(BOTH LAUGHING RAUCOUSLY)

38
00:02:12,933 --> 00:02:15,960
Hey, Harvey, has anyone
contacted you about Ra's al Ghul?

39
00:02:16,069 --> 00:02:17,069
No.

40
00:02:17,137 --> 00:02:18,615
I just heard from
Judge Bam Bam's clerk.

41
00:02:18,639 --> 00:02:20,801
- His trial got pushed off the docket.
- And?

42
00:02:22,309 --> 00:02:24,869
And I want to make sure, him
being minister of a foreign country,

43
00:02:24,978 --> 00:02:26,537
doesn't let him
weasel out of this.

44
00:02:26,847 --> 00:02:29,214
- He killed the boy.
- That's above my pay grade, pal.

45
00:02:29,316 --> 00:02:31,285
I just bust the bad guys.

46
00:02:32,686 --> 00:02:33,686
Do you?

47
00:02:35,589 --> 00:02:36,921
These are release forms.

48
00:02:37,991 --> 00:02:38,991
Of my collars.

49
00:02:39,092 --> 00:02:41,755
Let me guess, each one of them
has a license from Penguin, right?

50
00:02:41,828 --> 00:02:44,457
Jim, I am stuck between
a rock and a hard place.

51
00:02:44,531 --> 00:02:46,500
Every moop you
bust with a license,

52
00:02:46,600 --> 00:02:48,762
the Commissioner
orders me to let him go.

53
00:02:48,935 --> 00:02:50,130
What am I supposed to do?

54
00:02:50,370 --> 00:02:52,669
- Your job.
- I am doing my job.

55
00:02:53,206 --> 00:02:55,004
Gordon, got a call
from the judge's clerk.

56
00:02:55,208 --> 00:02:56,232
It's about Ra's al Ghul.

57
00:02:57,844 --> 00:03:00,211
- Here.
- I'm doing my job.

58
00:03:08,021 --> 00:03:09,045
Master Bruce.

59
00:03:10,791 --> 00:03:11,791
No sleep?

60
00:03:12,726 --> 00:03:13,726
Again?

61
00:03:17,698 --> 00:03:19,462
Once more about
that boy's death.

62
00:03:19,700 --> 00:03:21,532
Don't say it's not my fault.

63
00:03:22,002 --> 00:03:23,231
It is my fault.

64
00:03:23,603 --> 00:03:26,505
- Alex is dead because I hesitated.
- Well, perhaps you did,

65
00:03:26,573 --> 00:03:28,384
but that doesn't make
you his murderer, does it?

66
00:03:28,408 --> 00:03:32,004
Ra's killed that innocent little
boy and he's going to pay for it.

67
00:03:32,079 --> 00:03:34,399
You really think locking him
up in Blackgate will stop him?

68
00:03:34,448 --> 00:03:35,541
He still wants his dagger.

69
00:03:35,615 --> 00:03:37,326
Stop going on about the
bloody dagger, will you?

70
00:03:37,350 --> 00:03:39,649
Just so we can just get
some breakfast. Please.

71
00:03:39,720 --> 00:03:42,001
I think I finally found something
in Dr. Winthrop's notes.

72
00:03:42,222 --> 00:03:43,499
There's a description
on the handle

73
00:03:43,523 --> 00:03:45,253
that Dr. Winthrop
was able to decipher.

74
00:03:45,759 --> 00:03:47,489
Says the knife is
intended for the one

75
00:03:47,561 --> 00:03:49,257
who was bathed in
the healing waters.

76
00:03:49,930 --> 00:03:52,525
Right. Well, assuming that's not
me, that would be our boy Ra's.

77
00:03:52,699 --> 00:03:54,964
But that doesn't have to
mean it's for him to use.

78
00:03:55,902 --> 00:03:57,803
Perhaps to be used against him.

79
00:03:59,539 --> 00:04:01,303
- I see.
- No.

80
00:04:02,109 --> 00:04:03,109
You clearly don't.

81
00:04:03,210 --> 00:04:04,405
What you're suggesting is

82
00:04:04,478 --> 00:04:05,718
that knife and that knife alone

83
00:04:05,746 --> 00:04:07,386
is the only thing
capable of doing him in.

84
00:04:07,447 --> 00:04:09,541
If Ra's al Ghul believes
this knife will kill him,

85
00:04:09,783 --> 00:04:11,394
that could explain
why he wants it so bad.

86
00:04:11,418 --> 00:04:12,418
So he can destroy it.

87
00:04:14,221 --> 00:04:16,053
Before someone
fulfills the prophecy.

88
00:04:20,560 --> 00:04:23,962
Master Bruce, I know that you
feel bad about Alex, we all do.

89
00:04:25,098 --> 00:04:27,567
But at this point, you
must remember your vow.

90
00:04:30,604 --> 00:04:31,604
No killing.

91
00:04:32,973 --> 00:04:33,973
No killing.

92
00:04:35,776 --> 00:04:38,177
Taking a life, never
mind how justified,

93
00:04:38,278 --> 00:04:41,248
will lead you down a darker path
than you could ever possibly imagine.

94
00:04:41,648 --> 00:04:43,276
I know. I've been down it.

95
00:04:44,384 --> 00:04:46,615
- Do you understand me, Master Bruce?
- I understand.

96
00:04:47,921 --> 00:04:48,921
Good.

97
00:04:58,431 --> 00:04:59,592
Just get yourself ready.

98
00:05:00,700 --> 00:05:01,700
Chop-chop.

99
00:05:12,445 --> 00:05:13,606
WOMAN: Such a tragedy.

100
00:05:13,780 --> 00:05:17,080
He was only a child,
and always so lovely.

101
00:05:17,984 --> 00:05:18,984
A heinous crime,

102
00:05:19,686 --> 00:05:22,315
perpetrated against
such an innocent boy.

103
00:05:22,789 --> 00:05:27,227
WOMAN: And his grandfather,
murdered, just the day before.

104
00:05:34,501 --> 00:05:36,060
I'll just be a moment,
Master Bruce.

105
00:05:47,480 --> 00:05:48,607
Diplomatic immunity.

106
00:05:48,982 --> 00:05:50,348
You are joking, ain't you?

107
00:05:50,450 --> 00:05:53,648
The Nanda Parbat embassy
filed papers to have him extradited.

108
00:05:54,221 --> 00:05:56,656
- Could happen this week.
- The monster killed a child.

109
00:05:56,723 --> 00:05:59,158
I know. I was there. Look,

110
00:06:00,493 --> 00:06:02,086
I'm telling this
you as a courtesy.

111
00:06:02,395 --> 00:06:04,057
- Oh!
- But the news will get out.

112
00:06:04,164 --> 00:06:06,360
When it does, I need
you to watch Bruce.

113
00:06:06,900 --> 00:06:07,924
I'm worried about him.

114
00:06:08,535 --> 00:06:10,094
And you blame me?

115
00:06:10,337 --> 00:06:11,337
(SIGHS)

116
00:06:11,771 --> 00:06:13,069
You're his guardian, aren't you?

117
00:06:13,406 --> 00:06:14,646
You're supposed to protect him,

118
00:06:14,674 --> 00:06:16,666
and instead you've been
placing him in harm's way.

119
00:06:16,743 --> 00:06:19,008
ALFRED: Oh, I see.
So that's rankles, is it?

120
00:06:19,079 --> 00:06:20,079
Keeping you in the dark?

121
00:06:20,480 --> 00:06:22,847
Well, if I was you, I'd focus
on your own job, Detective,

122
00:06:22,916 --> 00:06:25,579
which is keeping Ra's al
Ghul behind bars, tucked up.

123
00:06:25,685 --> 00:06:27,630
Just keep the news away
from Bruce as long as you can.

124
00:06:27,654 --> 00:06:30,180
On that, we agree, Detective.

125
00:06:32,192 --> 00:06:33,455
The boy's been through enough.

126
00:06:39,566 --> 00:06:40,886
(RACY INSTRUMENTAL
MUSIC PLAYING)

127
00:06:48,708 --> 00:06:49,708
(LOCKER DOOR OPENING)

128
00:07:06,593 --> 00:07:07,959
(GATE BUZZING)

129
00:07:18,204 --> 00:07:19,570
Thanks for coming, Barbara.

130
00:07:19,739 --> 00:07:20,798
Hell of a chicken coop.

131
00:07:21,808 --> 00:07:22,867
So what's the angle?

132
00:07:25,445 --> 00:07:26,445
How about this?

133
00:07:28,148 --> 00:07:33,086
Say the word, we'll be home,
drinking Chianti by dinnertime.

134
00:07:33,820 --> 00:07:36,483
I think I'll decline.

135
00:07:38,758 --> 00:07:40,124
So why did you call me here?

136
00:07:40,827 --> 00:07:41,851
To say goodbye.

137
00:07:43,596 --> 00:07:44,928
When I brought you back to life,

138
00:07:45,465 --> 00:07:47,900
I asked you to be my
eyes and ears in Gotham.

139
00:07:49,469 --> 00:07:51,768
- You became so much more.
- Save it.

140
00:07:52,839 --> 00:07:54,569
What about everything
you promised me?

141
00:07:55,408 --> 00:07:59,607
Do as I ask, and I will give
you a gift beyond your imagining.

142
00:08:17,197 --> 00:08:18,197
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

143
00:08:23,803 --> 00:08:24,827
What the hell was that?

144
00:08:27,307 --> 00:08:28,307
You will see.

145
00:08:30,477 --> 00:08:31,604
Goodbye, Barbara.

146
00:08:46,493 --> 00:08:47,825
(DOOR SHUTS)

147
00:09:08,081 --> 00:09:09,392
(OMINOUS INSTRUMENTAL
MUSIC PLAYING)

148
00:09:09,416 --> 00:09:10,577
(GRUNTING)

149
00:09:22,929 --> 00:09:24,830
(SINGING) <i>Born on a Monday</i>

150
00:09:24,998 --> 00:09:26,933
<i>Christened on Tuesday</i>

151
00:09:27,333 --> 00:09:29,268
<i>Married on a Wednesday</i>

152
00:09:29,569 --> 00:09:31,265
<i>Took ill on Thursday</i>

153
00:09:31,738 --> 00:09:33,934
<i>Grew worse on Friday</i>

154
00:09:34,040 --> 00:09:36,373
<i>Died on Saturday</i>

155
00:09:36,443 --> 00:09:37,911
<i>Buried on...</i>

156
00:09:37,977 --> 00:09:39,206
Sweet mother of Mary.

157
00:09:41,047 --> 00:09:42,538
Never seen nothing
like him before.

158
00:09:43,416 --> 00:09:44,907
He's white as a picket fence.

159
00:09:45,485 --> 00:09:47,750
Easy. We ain't gonna hurt you.

160
00:09:48,655 --> 00:09:50,283
What happened to
your drawers, big fella?

161
00:09:50,490 --> 00:09:51,490
(SQUEALS)

162
00:09:51,591 --> 00:09:52,591
Easy.

163
00:09:55,995 --> 00:09:56,995
No!

164
00:09:57,464 --> 00:09:58,464
(GRUNTING)

165
00:10:03,303 --> 00:10:05,101
We're gonna get you, you freak.

166
00:10:05,738 --> 00:10:06,738
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

167
00:10:07,240 --> 00:10:09,903
(GASPING) Who are you?

168
00:10:11,111 --> 00:10:12,151
("SOLOMON GRUNDY" PLAYING)

169
00:10:27,794 --> 00:10:31,253
"Solomon Grundy.

170
00:10:32,899 --> 00:10:34,162
"Born...

171
00:10:35,835 --> 00:10:37,360
on Monday."

172
00:10:52,986 --> 00:10:56,650
License compliance amongst
the GCPD remains high.

173
00:10:57,524 --> 00:10:59,891
The program is an
unmitigated success.

174
00:10:59,993 --> 00:11:01,461
Numbers, Mr. Penn.

175
00:11:01,961 --> 00:11:03,623
According to my tabulations,

176
00:11:04,230 --> 00:11:08,190
86 percent of crime is
accounted for under Pax Penguina.

177
00:11:10,003 --> 00:11:11,995
Which means that 14
percent of crime happens

178
00:11:12,105 --> 00:11:13,835
outside of my licensing system.

179
00:11:15,475 --> 00:11:18,001
The numbers are very
good, Mr. Cobblepot.

180
00:11:18,945 --> 00:11:21,471
Get Firefly. I want
examples made.

181
00:11:21,548 --> 00:11:22,607
Yes, that might help.

182
00:11:24,551 --> 00:11:26,816
But then, if scorching a
few idiots was all it took,

183
00:11:26,886 --> 00:11:28,184
anyone could rule Gotham.

184
00:11:30,490 --> 00:11:32,152
Thank you for your
insight, Miss Falcone.

185
00:11:32,225 --> 00:11:33,659
I don't recall summoning you.

186
00:11:34,661 --> 00:11:36,721
I came to see if you had
lunch plans tomorrow.

187
00:11:39,032 --> 00:11:40,056
An invitation?

188
00:11:40,900 --> 00:11:41,900
(SCOFFS)

189
00:11:42,001 --> 00:11:46,268
After I killed your father's
last remaining loyalists?

190
00:11:46,372 --> 00:11:47,396
(CHUCKLES)

191
00:11:47,507 --> 00:11:50,204
Perhaps you overestimate
the pleasure of your company.

192
00:11:50,410 --> 00:11:51,410
Oswald.

193
00:11:52,745 --> 00:11:54,441
You may think
you have everything

194
00:11:55,014 --> 00:11:57,677
but there is one
thing you don't have.

195
00:11:58,751 --> 00:12:00,219
The Falcone name.

196
00:12:01,254 --> 00:12:05,282
A name that once accounted
for all criminal activity in Gotham.

197
00:12:05,592 --> 00:12:08,221
As in, one hundred percent.

198
00:12:10,930 --> 00:12:12,159
Now you're just rubbing it in.

199
00:12:13,766 --> 00:12:16,167
I propose we have
lunch somewhere public.

200
00:12:16,703 --> 00:12:18,171
By doing so, you'll show Gotham

201
00:12:18,238 --> 00:12:20,400
that you have the support
of the Falcone family.

202
00:12:20,940 --> 00:12:21,940
And that should be enough

203
00:12:22,041 --> 00:12:23,839
to send those outlying
criminal elements

204
00:12:23,910 --> 00:12:25,845
scurrying back
under your umbrella.

205
00:12:28,047 --> 00:12:31,040
Mr. Penn, item number
four on my to-do list.

206
00:12:34,921 --> 00:12:36,253
Kill Sofia Falcone.

207
00:12:39,892 --> 00:12:41,793
Add a question mark, will you?

208
00:12:44,230 --> 00:12:45,596
Tomorrow it is.

209
00:12:54,240 --> 00:12:56,232
God! Your people
have pills for everything!

210
00:12:56,609 --> 00:12:59,511
Insomnia. Anxiety. You have
to have something for me.

211
00:12:59,846 --> 00:13:01,486
I don't know. A pill
to reverse the effect

212
00:13:01,581 --> 00:13:03,277
of having your brain
frozen and unfrozen?

213
00:13:03,783 --> 00:13:04,944
That's kind of specific.

214
00:13:07,520 --> 00:13:11,753
I will not be condescended
to by an idiot in a lab coat!

215
00:13:12,625 --> 00:13:14,253
You're not even a doctor!

216
00:13:14,661 --> 00:13:17,654
Okay, relax, man. Just
tell me your symptoms.

217
00:13:18,831 --> 00:13:19,831
Fogginess of the mind,

218
00:13:20,733 --> 00:13:22,565
decreased capacity to
think ten steps ahead,

219
00:13:23,970 --> 00:13:25,461
inability to solve riddles.

220
00:13:27,006 --> 00:13:29,441
I have got to improve
my brain function.

221
00:13:30,076 --> 00:13:32,170
I could take a
pill or a vitamin.

222
00:13:32,745 --> 00:13:34,611
I'll even consider
a natural remedy.

223
00:13:34,981 --> 00:13:37,917
I don't want to get your hopes
up, but there is something.

224
00:13:38,251 --> 00:13:39,480
What? Tell me.

225
00:13:40,119 --> 00:13:41,143
A trial drug.

226
00:13:41,254 --> 00:13:44,156
It claims to boost your
natural cognitive abilities.

227
00:13:44,257 --> 00:13:46,488
- That's perfect! Where is this?
- The sample drawer.

228
00:13:48,161 --> 00:13:50,153
- What is it called?
- Smartivia.

229
00:13:50,363 --> 00:13:51,443
Blue pills. Diamond shaped.

230
00:13:51,664 --> 00:13:54,498
Smartivia. Smartivia.
I don't see them.

231
00:13:55,034 --> 00:13:56,127
Try towards the back.

232
00:13:56,736 --> 00:13:57,736
Ah! I don't see it.

233
00:13:59,072 --> 00:14:00,301
Here it is.

234
00:14:02,909 --> 00:14:04,901
(GROANING)

235
00:14:09,682 --> 00:14:11,708
A fake gun? Seriously?

236
00:14:13,686 --> 00:14:15,678
Wait, wait, wait. I
just need to know.

237
00:14:16,556 --> 00:14:17,556
Do these work?

238
00:14:17,790 --> 00:14:19,691
No, dummy. They're sugar pills.

239
00:14:19,892 --> 00:14:21,190
And I'm calling the police.

240
00:14:24,564 --> 00:14:25,644
(ALARM RINGING IN DISTANCE)

241
00:14:25,832 --> 00:14:26,832
Go on, gently.

242
00:14:29,369 --> 00:14:30,496
(GASPING)

243
00:14:35,641 --> 00:14:37,701
(SIRENS BLARING)

244
00:14:40,747 --> 00:14:41,908
(GROWLS)

245
00:14:42,014 --> 00:14:43,846
Ow! (PANTING)

246
00:14:49,389 --> 00:14:50,389
(GROWLS)

247
00:14:50,456 --> 00:14:51,456
(YELLS)

248
00:14:55,395 --> 00:14:56,395
Butch!

249
00:14:57,397 --> 00:14:59,866
You know Grundy?

250
00:15:00,133 --> 00:15:01,133
Butch.

251
00:15:01,467 --> 00:15:03,561
I have never had
an issue with you.

252
00:15:04,237 --> 00:15:05,728
Barbara Kean, she's the problem.

253
00:15:06,272 --> 00:15:08,138
You and Tabitha were
innocent bystanders.

254
00:15:08,441 --> 00:15:09,909
Wow. You don't get
much sun. Look...

255
00:15:13,813 --> 00:15:15,372
Man talk too much.

256
00:15:21,621 --> 00:15:23,351
- Collins. Deal with this, will you?
- Yep.

257
00:15:23,689 --> 00:15:25,749
Gordon. Gordon!

258
00:15:26,726 --> 00:15:28,058
- Bruce is gone.
- What?

259
00:15:28,561 --> 00:15:30,873
- You've got to get me into Blackgate.
- What are you talking about?

260
00:15:30,897 --> 00:15:32,107
When we got back from the wake,

261
00:15:32,131 --> 00:15:33,409
he said he was gonna
go straight to bed,

262
00:15:33,433 --> 00:15:35,368
but he must have snuck
out between then and now.

263
00:15:35,435 --> 00:15:37,768
My concern is that
he's taken the knife...

264
00:15:38,938 --> 00:15:40,600
and he's gonna try
and kill Ra's al Ghul.

265
00:15:42,575 --> 00:15:44,976
- You're serious?
- He's being bloody serious.

266
00:15:45,311 --> 00:15:46,802
We gotta go to Blackgate now.

267
00:15:47,313 --> 00:15:48,804
And then you can
tell me the many ways

268
00:15:48,915 --> 00:15:50,281
I failed the child, all right?

269
00:15:50,349 --> 00:15:52,147
- Oh, I will.
- Listen to me.

270
00:15:52,852 --> 00:15:54,692
The boy is on the verge
of doing something that

271
00:15:54,787 --> 00:15:55,982
there's no coming back from.

272
00:15:57,690 --> 00:15:58,690
He needs our help.

273
00:16:00,993 --> 00:16:01,993
All right.

274
00:16:02,762 --> 00:16:03,762
Let's go.

275
00:16:07,099 --> 00:16:08,099
(DOGS BARKING)

276
00:16:11,838 --> 00:16:13,198
(TENSE INSTRUMENTAL
MUSIC PLAYING)

277
00:16:30,122 --> 00:16:32,956
It's about time. Shift
ended five minutes ago.

278
00:16:33,326 --> 00:16:34,326
Come on.

279
00:17:18,704 --> 00:17:20,264
(ENTHRALLING
INSTRUMENTAL MUSIC PLAYING)

280
00:17:46,832 --> 00:17:48,061
You weak,

281
00:17:49,201 --> 00:17:52,171
foolish boy.

282
00:17:57,276 --> 00:17:58,437
(GRUNTS)

283
00:17:58,644 --> 00:17:59,873
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

284
00:18:02,248 --> 00:18:03,248
(GASPING)

285
00:18:07,219 --> 00:18:08,744
You're still not ready.

286
00:18:19,632 --> 00:18:21,624
My name is Bruce
Wayne. Stop him!

287
00:18:22,802 --> 00:18:23,802
Stop him!

288
00:18:27,607 --> 00:18:28,607
Master al Ghul.

289
00:18:30,910 --> 00:18:31,910
Take him below.

290
00:18:33,245 --> 00:18:34,440
What... what are you doing?

291
00:18:42,822 --> 00:18:43,822
(DOOR BUZZING)

292
00:18:43,990 --> 00:18:45,390
We got your call,

293
00:18:46,092 --> 00:18:47,970
but I checked the logs.
Bruce Wayne hasn't been here.

294
00:18:47,994 --> 00:18:50,725
With all due respect, I don't
think he'd come as a regular visitor.

295
00:18:50,963 --> 00:18:52,431
He's a billionaire, after all.

296
00:18:52,498 --> 00:18:54,899
I think what Mr. Pennyworth
is trying to say

297
00:18:54,967 --> 00:18:57,459
is Bruce Wayne could have
paid someone to get him in here.

298
00:18:57,803 --> 00:18:58,803
No offense.

299
00:18:59,305 --> 00:19:00,466
We just want to look around.

300
00:19:02,541 --> 00:19:04,442
Sure. Whatever you want.

301
00:19:05,144 --> 00:19:06,784
But you came all the
way here for nothing.

302
00:19:07,279 --> 00:19:08,975
And we're gonna
need your weapons.

303
00:19:11,817 --> 00:19:12,817
Standard procedure.

304
00:19:14,153 --> 00:19:15,153
Of course.

305
00:19:19,191 --> 00:19:20,191
(CLEARS THROAT)

306
00:19:24,063 --> 00:19:25,063
(CLEARS THROAT)

307
00:19:37,777 --> 00:19:39,302
- Finished?
- That's absolutely it.

308
00:19:39,378 --> 00:19:41,347
Unless you wanna
check my undercrackers.

309
00:19:43,449 --> 00:19:44,449
This way.

310
00:19:45,551 --> 00:19:46,551
Undercrackers?

311
00:19:52,358 --> 00:19:53,358
They're here.

312
00:20:02,768 --> 00:20:03,768
(GROANING)

313
00:20:13,179 --> 00:20:15,273
Sugar pills, my foot.

314
00:20:16,716 --> 00:20:18,048
That dream was horrible.

315
00:20:19,085 --> 00:20:21,520
Oh, my God! Oh, you're real.

316
00:20:21,754 --> 00:20:22,754
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

317
00:20:24,223 --> 00:20:28,388
You know Grundy?

318
00:20:28,594 --> 00:20:30,062
What? No. No.

319
00:20:30,529 --> 00:20:31,529
No, who's Grundy?

320
00:20:32,698 --> 00:20:34,098
Solomon Grundy.

321
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,593
Born on Monday.

322
00:20:37,937 --> 00:20:39,405
Your hand. How...

323
00:20:40,506 --> 00:20:43,203
I'm sorry, what happened to you?

324
00:20:45,611 --> 00:20:46,840
Grundy not know.

325
00:20:48,714 --> 00:20:51,707
Okay, let me get this
straight. You don't remember...

326
00:20:52,618 --> 00:20:55,349
who you are or how you got here?

327
00:21:00,726 --> 00:21:01,726
I'm sorry.

328
00:21:02,094 --> 00:21:04,393
Grundy, I don't know you.

329
00:21:05,664 --> 00:21:06,664
Best of luck, though.

330
00:21:06,766 --> 00:21:08,667
Hope you get the skin
thing figured out. Later.

331
00:21:08,801 --> 00:21:09,801
(SCREAMING)

332
00:21:12,238 --> 00:21:14,969
You know Grundy.

333
00:21:15,241 --> 00:21:17,233
You help Grundy.

334
00:21:17,610 --> 00:21:21,911
Be Grundy friend.

335
00:21:24,450 --> 00:21:25,941
I'm attempting to be civil.

336
00:21:27,319 --> 00:21:28,480
But I can't help you.

337
00:21:29,522 --> 00:21:30,522
Why?

338
00:21:30,823 --> 00:21:32,416
I just can't. All right?

339
00:21:32,658 --> 00:21:33,921
- Why?
- Because...

340
00:21:34,126 --> 00:21:37,460
- Why?
- Because I can't even help myself.

341
00:21:38,063 --> 00:21:39,122
Ow!

342
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:45,059
You don't know who you
are. Well, that makes two of us.

343
00:21:45,738 --> 00:21:47,104
I used to be smart.

344
00:21:47,940 --> 00:21:48,964
Brilliant.

345
00:21:50,242 --> 00:21:51,471
And now that's gone.

346
00:21:51,844 --> 00:21:53,745
I can't even rob a pharmacy.

347
00:21:54,814 --> 00:21:57,113
So you want me to help you?

348
00:21:59,084 --> 00:22:00,084
I can't.

349
00:22:00,753 --> 00:22:01,753
(BREATHING HEAVILY)

350
00:22:15,301 --> 00:22:16,963
Well, I am feeling
a bit peckish.

351
00:22:27,713 --> 00:22:28,874
We are closed.

352
00:22:29,248 --> 00:22:30,375
Janos.

353
00:22:32,084 --> 00:22:34,144
Last I saw you was
at my tenth birthday.

354
00:22:34,220 --> 00:22:35,813
You bought me ruby earrings.

355
00:22:36,355 --> 00:22:37,432
Said it would be a fitting gift

356
00:22:37,456 --> 00:22:39,220
for the daughter of
the king of Gotham.

357
00:22:41,327 --> 00:22:42,556
Sofia Falcone.

358
00:22:43,462 --> 00:22:45,055
I heard you had
returned to Gotham.

359
00:22:45,831 --> 00:22:46,890
What can I do for you?

360
00:22:48,367 --> 00:22:50,836
I was wondering how you
were faring under Penguin's rule.

361
00:22:52,204 --> 00:22:53,900
The Szabo family
is quite content

362
00:22:54,006 --> 00:22:56,498
under Oswald Cobblepot's
licensing system.

363
00:22:57,009 --> 00:22:58,637
But even if we were not,

364
00:22:59,478 --> 00:23:01,640
we would be wise
enough to not say anything.

365
00:23:02,915 --> 00:23:03,915
Good.

366
00:23:04,149 --> 00:23:06,414
Because I've invited him
to your restaurant for lunch.

367
00:23:07,119 --> 00:23:09,679
And I want it to be a
lunch he'll never forget.

368
00:23:12,358 --> 00:23:13,718
(FUNKY INSTRUMENTAL
MUSIC PLAYING)

369
00:23:27,539 --> 00:23:28,539
RA'S: Bruce...

370
00:23:36,248 --> 00:23:37,248
Where am I?

371
00:23:38,183 --> 00:23:39,913
Beneath Blackgate Penitentiary.

372
00:23:41,186 --> 00:23:45,089
Alfred Pennyworth and
Jim Gordon are upstairs.

373
00:23:45,758 --> 00:23:49,388
In the company, unbeknownst
to them, of my men.

374
00:23:49,461 --> 00:23:52,056
Let them go. They have
nothing to do with this.

375
00:23:52,264 --> 00:23:55,428
Still playing the
white knight, Bruce?

376
00:23:55,601 --> 00:23:57,536
You replaced the
guards before I got here.

377
00:23:57,703 --> 00:24:00,036
I'm sure your friends
can fend for themselves.

378
00:24:00,105 --> 00:24:03,075
You applied for diplomatic
immunity, knowing I'd hear about it.

379
00:24:04,076 --> 00:24:05,076
And come for you.

380
00:24:05,377 --> 00:24:06,377
I wanted the knife.

381
00:24:07,546 --> 00:24:08,980
But not for the
reason you think.

382
00:24:12,017 --> 00:24:15,351
It's been ages since I
first held this dagger.

383
00:24:16,355 --> 00:24:19,086
It was given to me
moments after I was bathed

384
00:24:19,158 --> 00:24:20,421
in the Lazarus Pit.

385
00:24:22,161 --> 00:24:24,528
Submerged in the waters.

386
00:24:27,199 --> 00:24:28,199
(GASPING)

387
00:24:33,105 --> 00:24:38,009
Suspended between
life and death.

388
00:24:39,845 --> 00:24:41,438
I saw a vision of you,

389
00:24:44,016 --> 00:24:45,109
my heir.

390
00:24:47,353 --> 00:24:48,480
You're insane.

391
00:24:49,521 --> 00:24:51,183
I'm not your heir. I
don't even understand

392
00:24:51,290 --> 00:24:52,290
what that means.

393
00:24:52,358 --> 00:24:55,453
It means that you
are the only one

394
00:24:55,828 --> 00:24:58,263
who can end my suffering.

395
00:25:03,002 --> 00:25:04,002
Please.

396
00:25:06,672 --> 00:25:08,140
You want me to kill you?

397
00:25:10,476 --> 00:25:11,705
Set me free.

398
00:25:22,921 --> 00:25:24,361
Well, thanks for
the snack, big guy.

399
00:25:25,924 --> 00:25:27,187
But it's been an emotional day.

400
00:25:28,727 --> 00:25:29,727
Gotta go.

401
00:25:30,763 --> 00:25:31,763
(EXCLAIMS)

402
00:25:32,431 --> 00:25:33,990
Not this again, come on!

403
00:25:35,667 --> 00:25:38,102
I've told you, I'm
better off on my own

404
00:25:38,504 --> 00:25:39,665
and you are, too.

405
00:25:39,872 --> 00:25:41,033
So let go!

406
00:25:41,540 --> 00:25:42,906
Let go!

407
00:25:43,208 --> 00:25:44,208
Hey, freak.

408
00:25:45,577 --> 00:25:46,577
I knew we'd find you.

409
00:25:47,012 --> 00:25:48,537
And it looks like
you got a friend.

410
00:25:49,648 --> 00:25:52,174
I assure you, we
are not friends.

411
00:25:53,218 --> 00:25:54,686
Get 'em. Both of 'em.

412
00:25:54,887 --> 00:25:55,887
No, no!

413
00:25:56,321 --> 00:25:57,321
(GRUNTING AND GROANING)

414
00:26:06,832 --> 00:26:07,832
Grundy!

415
00:26:09,168 --> 00:26:10,168
(SCREAMING)

416
00:26:11,503 --> 00:26:13,096
Hot! Hot!

417
00:26:13,639 --> 00:26:14,732
Grundy friend, help!

418
00:26:15,407 --> 00:26:17,137
Don't leave. No. Help!

419
00:26:17,242 --> 00:26:20,440
Help. Hot. Hot!

420
00:26:21,080 --> 00:26:22,080
Hot!

421
00:26:24,083 --> 00:26:25,083
(GROANING)

422
00:26:28,153 --> 00:26:29,314
Grundy friend not dumb.

423
00:26:31,156 --> 00:26:32,156
Grundy friend...

424
00:26:33,325 --> 00:26:34,325
smart.

425
00:26:34,827 --> 00:26:35,827
Oh, yes.

426
00:26:36,895 --> 00:26:38,056
Yeah, you're right.

427
00:26:38,831 --> 00:26:40,766
Water beats fire. (LAUGHS)

428
00:26:41,333 --> 00:26:42,392
That was smart.

429
00:26:44,536 --> 00:26:45,536
Oh, boy.

430
00:26:48,273 --> 00:26:49,313
(GASPING) I can't breathe.

431
00:27:02,888 --> 00:27:03,888
Oswald.

432
00:27:04,456 --> 00:27:06,948
- They said this is their best table.
- Interesting choice.

433
00:27:08,460 --> 00:27:10,053
Are you sure it's
not too intimate?

434
00:27:10,796 --> 00:27:13,391
The point was to get the word
out that the Falcones support me.

435
00:27:14,233 --> 00:27:15,701
Don't worry. People will talk.

436
00:27:19,638 --> 00:27:22,267
I chose this place because I
heard your mother is Hungarian.

437
00:27:22,508 --> 00:27:24,136
I thought you might
like a taste of home.

438
00:27:24,610 --> 00:27:25,610
(SCOFFS)

439
00:27:44,530 --> 00:27:47,193
I can assure you, Oswald,
I'm not here to poison you.

440
00:27:48,433 --> 00:27:49,433
Perhaps.

441
00:27:49,501 --> 00:27:50,525
(COUGHS)

442
00:27:52,704 --> 00:27:55,105
Well, the chef likes to go
heavy on the paprika, doesn't he?

443
00:27:56,508 --> 00:27:58,306
How is the food otherwise?

444
00:27:59,478 --> 00:28:00,502
Serviceable.

445
00:28:04,383 --> 00:28:08,115
Well, I'm stuffed. Thank you so
much for meeting me, Miss Falcone.

446
00:28:08,187 --> 00:28:10,122
And thank you to your
family for their support.

447
00:28:10,489 --> 00:28:12,390
You can't leave until
you've tried the goulash.

448
00:28:12,824 --> 00:28:15,794
If it's anything like the
chicken paprika, I'll pass.

449
00:28:15,994 --> 00:28:17,053
It's a house specialty.

450
00:28:26,572 --> 00:28:27,699
My mother made goulash.

451
00:28:28,907 --> 00:28:30,239
Brought the recipe
from Budapest.

452
00:28:30,409 --> 00:28:33,004
Handed down through
her family for 300 years.

453
00:28:35,948 --> 00:28:37,883
I doubt this will hold a candle.

454
00:29:01,773 --> 00:29:02,773
(GRUNTS)

455
00:29:03,175 --> 00:29:04,837
- I'm leaving.
- Oswald.

456
00:29:06,612 --> 00:29:07,612
Oswald!

457
00:29:12,351 --> 00:29:14,377
It took me forever to
find his mother's recipe.

458
00:29:14,453 --> 00:29:15,944
Did you follow it exactly?

459
00:29:16,221 --> 00:29:18,349
I followed the recipe to a T.

460
00:29:18,957 --> 00:29:20,448
The little man didn't like?

461
00:29:21,960 --> 00:29:23,326
Honestly, I don't know.

462
00:29:29,801 --> 00:29:31,001
How long have you worked here?

463
00:29:31,570 --> 00:29:33,562
Two years, thereabouts.

464
00:29:34,406 --> 00:29:35,840
I was in Blackgate for a time.

465
00:29:36,341 --> 00:29:38,242
- We must not have overlapped.
- Yeah?

466
00:29:38,944 --> 00:29:40,936
- As a guard?
- As a prisoner.

467
00:29:42,347 --> 00:29:43,347
Oh, yeah.

468
00:29:43,749 --> 00:29:44,749
Heard about that.

469
00:29:44,983 --> 00:29:47,680
Is there a reason why you're not
taking us through maximum security?

470
00:29:47,953 --> 00:29:49,945
Prisoners are in the
yard this time of day.

471
00:29:51,290 --> 00:29:52,883
Been some changes
since you were here.

472
00:29:56,395 --> 00:29:58,955
McCloskey? That's funny.

473
00:29:59,898 --> 00:30:02,265
I know another J.
McCloskey who works here.

474
00:30:04,670 --> 00:30:07,003
My cousin. Gets
confusing sometimes.

475
00:30:07,806 --> 00:30:10,332
All right. Let's go,
through this door.

476
00:30:10,742 --> 00:30:13,454
I've got to say, mate, I really love
what you've done with the old place.

477
00:30:13,478 --> 00:30:15,447
However, I've got
a question for you.

478
00:30:17,115 --> 00:30:18,115
Yeah?

479
00:30:18,784 --> 00:30:19,945
Where are the real guards?

480
00:30:20,585 --> 00:30:21,665
(ALL GRUNTING AND GROANING)

481
00:30:36,034 --> 00:30:37,366
Where is Bruce Wayne?

482
00:30:38,470 --> 00:30:40,837
- Ra's al Ghul has plans for the boy.
- Where is he?

483
00:30:41,239 --> 00:30:43,140
(CHUCKLES)
You'll never find him.

484
00:30:43,975 --> 00:30:46,240
Oh, you underestimate
my resolve, pal.

485
00:30:52,751 --> 00:30:54,276
Well, at least we
know Bruce is here.

486
00:30:54,386 --> 00:30:56,287
Well, we've walked the
floor. Where could he be?

487
00:30:56,488 --> 00:30:57,488
There's the yard.

488
00:30:58,123 --> 00:30:59,648
The tower, but
they're too public.

489
00:31:01,126 --> 00:31:03,493
There's a sub-basement.
Accessible by the service elevator.

490
00:31:03,662 --> 00:31:04,662
Which way?

491
00:31:16,141 --> 00:31:17,141
(DOOR OPENS)

492
00:31:21,813 --> 00:31:22,813
God.

493
00:31:23,582 --> 00:31:26,211
Who did I tell you,
specifically, not to let in here?

494
00:31:27,386 --> 00:31:29,355
Miss Falcone is
here to see you, sir.

495
00:31:32,257 --> 00:31:34,954
I'm sorry, Oswald. I'm not
sure what upset you, but...

496
00:31:35,060 --> 00:31:36,060
Enough!

497
00:31:36,962 --> 00:31:40,057
Did you think I would really believe
this was all some coincidence?

498
00:31:41,099 --> 00:31:43,762
That goulash tasted exactly
like my mother used to make.

499
00:31:44,436 --> 00:31:46,701
You can't fault me for the
restaurant's authenticity.

500
00:31:47,739 --> 00:31:49,071
You're buttering me up.

501
00:31:49,875 --> 00:31:50,875
But for what?

502
00:31:52,277 --> 00:31:53,802
Is it so hard to believe that

503
00:31:53,912 --> 00:31:56,211
someone would want to
do something nice for you?

504
00:31:56,281 --> 00:31:57,892
There was only one
person in my whole life

505
00:31:57,916 --> 00:32:00,396
who ever did things for me
without wanting something in return.

506
00:32:01,253 --> 00:32:02,380
And that was my mother.

507
00:32:03,255 --> 00:32:04,348
Then I envy you.

508
00:32:05,924 --> 00:32:08,689
My father never helped
anyone unless it benefited him.

509
00:32:09,361 --> 00:32:11,796
And eventually, it drove
away everyone who loved him.

510
00:32:15,600 --> 00:32:18,536
Go. I'll decide what
to do with you later.

511
00:32:22,808 --> 00:32:26,108
- Oswald, I only want to help you.
- Oh, you wanna help?

512
00:32:26,411 --> 00:32:27,411
Try leaving.

513
00:32:27,512 --> 00:32:28,512
(SCOFFS)

514
00:32:30,081 --> 00:32:31,081
Your foot.

515
00:32:32,317 --> 00:32:33,410
It's just the weather.

516
00:32:35,253 --> 00:32:36,253
(BREATHING SHAKILY)

517
00:32:42,127 --> 00:32:43,127
What are you doing?

518
00:32:46,198 --> 00:32:47,461
- Don't.
- (SOFTLY) It's okay.

519
00:32:48,667 --> 00:32:49,760
And I won't judge.

520
00:33:11,323 --> 00:33:14,691
When I was a child, I broke my
ankle while playing with my cousins.

521
00:33:16,428 --> 00:33:20,524
I was desperate. Crying in pain.

522
00:33:21,800 --> 00:33:23,496
My father told
me to put ice on it.

523
00:33:24,269 --> 00:33:26,135
Toughen up, stop with the tears.

524
00:33:27,439 --> 00:33:29,203
But my mother went
with me to the hospital.

525
00:33:30,342 --> 00:33:31,901
And on the way, she told me

526
00:33:32,010 --> 00:33:34,411
that cold actually
increases the pain.

527
00:33:36,915 --> 00:33:38,645
What's needed is warmth.

528
00:33:43,488 --> 00:33:44,488
My mother.

529
00:33:45,891 --> 00:33:47,052
She used to sing.

530
00:33:49,995 --> 00:33:50,995
(HUMMING)

531
00:34:10,248 --> 00:34:13,480
RA'S: This may be hard
for you to understand.

532
00:34:15,987 --> 00:34:19,082
But I have walked this
earth for centuries...

533
00:34:19,925 --> 00:34:21,826
waiting for you, Bruce.

534
00:34:23,361 --> 00:34:24,886
Only you can kill me,

535
00:34:25,597 --> 00:34:27,395
and only with that dagger.

536
00:34:28,733 --> 00:34:30,201
That is my curse.

537
00:34:31,469 --> 00:34:33,028
That is the meaning
of my vision.

538
00:34:34,606 --> 00:34:35,767
I don't believe you.

539
00:34:36,408 --> 00:34:39,572
- Believe me.
- This is just another manipulation.

540
00:34:41,947 --> 00:34:42,947
See.

541
00:34:44,749 --> 00:34:45,749
Look.

542
00:34:46,551 --> 00:34:47,780
My true form.

543
00:34:50,255 --> 00:34:53,089
Every moment
of my life is agony.

544
00:34:56,761 --> 00:34:57,956
End my suffering.

545
00:35:00,565 --> 00:35:01,794
Whatever your curse is,

546
00:35:04,369 --> 00:35:06,270
you deserve it for
what you've done.

547
00:35:06,438 --> 00:35:08,771
You're angry,
Bruce. I understand.

548
00:35:09,374 --> 00:35:11,104
But unless you strike me down

549
00:35:11,209 --> 00:35:13,235
with that blade, you
will never be free.

550
00:35:13,311 --> 00:35:14,311
No!

551
00:35:16,548 --> 00:35:17,548
I won't.

552
00:35:20,251 --> 00:35:22,379
Then allow me to tell
you what will happen...

553
00:35:24,122 --> 00:35:25,750
if you don't kill me.

554
00:35:28,660 --> 00:35:29,923
I will disappear.

555
00:35:31,396 --> 00:35:33,331
And let you live your life.

556
00:35:34,633 --> 00:35:37,501
You will follow
the path of light.

557
00:35:38,436 --> 00:35:41,804
Grow into a fine man.
Become a husband.

558
00:35:43,274 --> 00:35:44,274
A father.

559
00:35:45,877 --> 00:35:48,005
There may be a
day when you forget

560
00:35:48,680 --> 00:35:50,046
I ever existed.

561
00:35:53,518 --> 00:35:56,488
But then, I will return.

562
00:35:57,689 --> 00:36:01,558
And I will kill
everyone you love.

563
00:36:02,494 --> 00:36:05,123
Just as you watched
your parents die.

564
00:36:05,530 --> 00:36:09,865
Just as you watched me
slice your friend's throat,

565
00:36:10,435 --> 00:36:16,102
I will slaughter your wife and
children before your very eyes

566
00:36:16,174 --> 00:36:19,770
and there will be nothing
you can do about it.

567
00:36:20,545 --> 00:36:21,545
(GRUNTING AND GASPING)

568
00:36:23,381 --> 00:36:24,381
Die.

569
00:36:24,983 --> 00:36:25,983
(SCREAMING)

570
00:36:44,602 --> 00:36:46,093
Yes. (BREATHING HEAVILY)

571
00:37:16,000 --> 00:37:17,040
(INDISTINCT ANNOUNCEMENTS)

572
00:37:27,679 --> 00:37:28,840
Are you going to arrest me?

573
00:37:30,415 --> 00:37:31,415
For what?

574
00:37:33,952 --> 00:37:34,952
For murder.

575
00:37:35,687 --> 00:37:37,246
I don't know what
I just saw in there.

576
00:37:37,789 --> 00:37:38,866
But as far as I'm concerned,

577
00:37:38,890 --> 00:37:41,917
Ra's al Ghul's men broke
into Blackgate and he escaped.

578
00:37:44,162 --> 00:37:46,631
I betrayed myself, and
my parents' memory.

579
00:37:49,300 --> 00:37:50,734
I took a life.

580
00:37:51,503 --> 00:37:53,301
I did exactly what
Ra's said I would.

581
00:37:54,606 --> 00:37:56,751
Just because you know you're
capable of doing something

582
00:37:56,775 --> 00:37:58,334
doesn't mean it
has to happen again.

583
00:38:01,412 --> 00:38:03,643
Bruce, you and I have
known each other a long time.

584
00:38:04,916 --> 00:38:06,748
Since the night your
parents were murdered.

585
00:38:07,619 --> 00:38:09,463
Now you may not feel
like you're that kid anymore,

586
00:38:09,487 --> 00:38:10,785
but I know that you are.

587
00:38:12,223 --> 00:38:13,816
One who believes in doing good,

588
00:38:15,260 --> 00:38:16,489
and fighting for what's right,

589
00:38:18,496 --> 00:38:21,091
who will do anything to
keep the people he loves safe.

590
00:38:23,601 --> 00:38:27,060
Nothing that happened
today changes that.

591
00:38:40,819 --> 00:38:41,819
What are you doing?

592
00:38:42,520 --> 00:38:43,520
You said it yourself.

593
00:38:45,557 --> 00:38:46,557
It's over.

594
00:38:48,193 --> 00:38:49,193
No.

595
00:38:50,128 --> 00:38:52,154
- Can't let you do that, Master Bruce.
- Alfred.

596
00:38:52,564 --> 00:38:54,499
Listen, we started
this vigilante caper

597
00:38:54,566 --> 00:38:56,831
to prepare for Ra's
return, didn't we?

598
00:38:58,369 --> 00:38:59,894
It's become so
much bigger than that.

599
00:39:00,672 --> 00:39:03,232
I see that now, I mean, I
was wrong and you were right.

600
00:39:05,076 --> 00:39:06,374
You can make a difference.

601
00:39:10,315 --> 00:39:12,147
I'm not the hero Gotham needs.

602
00:39:13,885 --> 00:39:16,878
I made that decision the
moment I killed Ra's al Ghul.

603
00:39:19,490 --> 00:39:20,788
I took the dark path.

604
00:39:23,561 --> 00:39:24,561
Yes, you did.

605
00:39:25,663 --> 00:39:28,189
And it's gonna be a
long, bumpy journey back.

606
00:39:29,801 --> 00:39:34,671
But I believe in you, Master Bruce.
I always have and I... I always will.

607
00:39:36,908 --> 00:39:39,173
And I understand that
you don't feel worthy now.

608
00:39:40,378 --> 00:39:42,779
But when you do, this...

609
00:39:45,717 --> 00:39:46,912
this will be waiting for you.

610
00:39:50,688 --> 00:39:52,554
As will I, sir.

611
00:40:14,679 --> 00:40:15,723
These guys that attacked us,

612
00:40:15,747 --> 00:40:17,716
they didn't even have
five bucks between them.

613
00:40:18,750 --> 00:40:19,911
We need a new plan.

614
00:40:25,790 --> 00:40:26,790
What?

615
00:40:27,959 --> 00:40:28,959
Truth.

616
00:40:29,861 --> 00:40:32,456
Grundy friend know...

617
00:40:33,298 --> 00:40:34,298
Grundy?

618
00:40:36,100 --> 00:40:37,568
You deserve to know...

619
00:40:38,803 --> 00:40:39,930
you and I,

620
00:40:41,539 --> 00:40:42,539
(SIGHS)

621
00:40:44,042 --> 00:40:46,011
were the very best of friends.

622
00:40:46,678 --> 00:40:48,237
And then something
happened to you

623
00:40:48,613 --> 00:40:49,790
and I just didn't recognize you.

624
00:40:49,814 --> 00:40:53,342
But what is important is
that with your muscles,

625
00:40:54,118 --> 00:40:55,245
we can make money.

626
00:40:56,187 --> 00:40:59,248
And with money, we
can make me smart again.

627
00:41:00,258 --> 00:41:02,124
And then we'll figure out
what happened to you.

628
00:41:02,961 --> 00:41:04,793
Just trust me, okay?

629
00:41:09,467 --> 00:41:10,467
Grundy, come on.

630
00:41:11,803 --> 00:41:12,827
(ROCK MUSIC PLAYING)

631
00:41:13,371 --> 00:41:14,651
(PEOPLE CHATTERING AND CHEERING)

632
00:41:18,977 --> 00:41:19,977
(PUNCHES THUMPING)

633
00:41:28,152 --> 00:41:29,152
(GRUNTING)

634
00:41:30,755 --> 00:41:31,755
Yeah, come on!

635
00:41:45,503 --> 00:41:48,337
What is this? A knitting
circle? Let's see some blood!

636
00:41:49,640 --> 00:41:51,480
Hey, I'm looking for the
person in charge here.

637
00:41:52,877 --> 00:41:53,877
You're looking at her.

638
00:41:55,246 --> 00:41:56,339
What do you want, squirt?

639
00:41:57,515 --> 00:42:00,383
Well, if there's money to be had,
we'd like to put our hat in the ring.

640
00:42:00,585 --> 00:42:01,585
(LAUGHS SARCASTICALLY)

641
00:42:02,420 --> 00:42:03,420
And who are you?

642
00:42:04,055 --> 00:42:05,079
I'm... Hey!

643
00:42:05,390 --> 00:42:06,390
Come back.

644
00:42:07,492 --> 00:42:10,052
I'm this fine
gentleman's manager.

645
00:42:10,828 --> 00:42:12,990
Trust me, he's a monster.

646
00:42:13,598 --> 00:42:16,864
Well, more grist for the mill.

647
00:42:19,337 --> 00:42:21,568
We'll get you patched
up. Then we'll talk.

648
00:42:22,573 --> 00:42:23,573
Hey!

649
00:42:24,308 --> 00:42:25,308
Go get the doc.

650
00:42:27,378 --> 00:42:29,506
All right. One, two, three.

651
00:42:35,653 --> 00:42:38,418
Hey, doc! Cherry wants you
to come look at some new guy.

652
00:42:39,390 --> 00:42:40,517
WOMAN: I'll be right there.

653
00:43:34,579 --> 00:43:35,579
English - SDH
